 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, internal reference (RBIAS, EXTREF), out-of-range detection",
  "conversion time is the Table 9 settling time after START (fCLK = 7.3728 MHz, DELAY = 000) for every conversion; continuous gate-mode conversions after the first run at 1 / data rate (10 SPS to 14.4 kSPS); DELAY[2:0] start delay (Table 8) not added",
  "RDATAC mode (default): the data are the default output pattern R{24} at every transaction start and repeat while SCLKs continue; in SDATAC mode the device does not shift data without RDATA (the model still shifts R{24} until a command reply replaces it); DOUT follows DRDY with CS low only in RDATAC mode (modeled)",
  "commands other than SDATAC are decoded in RDATAC mode as well (the datasheet requires SDATAC first)",
  "checksum byte (CONFIG1.CHKSUM, sum of the data bytes + 9Bh) and out-of-range flag (CONFIG1.FLAG) are stored only, never output",
  "DRDY (gate mode) returns high on the first SCLK of a read; 20 tCLK update window and the DRDY high pulse when data are not read",
  "RESET/PWDN held low powers the device down (modeled as reset held)",
  "OFSCAL / GANCAL calibrations (OFC/FSC not updated)",
  "SLEEP mode wake-up time; SPI timeout (CONFIG0.SPI, SCLK low 2^16 tCLK, printed as 216 in the text layout); START/STOP take effect on the 7th SCLK falling edge (modeled at the 8th)",
  "SYNCOUT clock output (fCLK/8), crystal / external clock (CONFIG2.EXTCLK stays 0)"
